llection of Énrico Ragusa was in the Instituto di Zoologia, Universita di Napoli, Portici, Italy (ZIUP); at our request Roberta Improta made a thorough search of the Naples Museum collections but was unable to find any of Ragusa’s M. phoebe specimens (see Acknowledgements). From the NHM specimens, which are clearly M. ornata, a male captured by Ragusa in the District of Palermo is herewith designated as a lectotype. The specific characters of ornata are clearly visible in the photographs of the lectotype (Figs 13 a, b). M. phoebe has not been reported from Sicily (RUSSELL, 2018). The labels on the pin of the lectotype (Fig. 13 c) are as follows: on beige paper, part printed part handwritten “ Prov. Palermo / Local. V [all] Corta / Data 10.5. [1] 917 / Coll. E. Ragusa ”; on beige paper, printed “ Sicily, / coll. E. Ragusa ”; on purple-bordered circular white paper printed “ LECTO- / TYPE ”; on beige paper printed “ Rothschild / Bequest / B. M. 1939 - 1. ”; on white paper printed “ LECTOTYPE / Melitaea phoebe forma / punicata Ragusa, 1919 / Designated by Russell / & Tennent, 2019 ”.","","text","",""]]},"V56YP":{"d":[["Tennessee","48472","mrgid","",""]]},"V5MKG":{"d":[["GY","GY","iso","",""],["VEN","VE","iso","",""]]},"V6G5B":{"d":[["Caribbean","","text","",""]]},"V82J":{"d":[["Tanganyika, Lake","18520","mrgid","",""]]},"V8SV3":{"d":[["Distribution. Thailand (Fig. 32 d).","","text","",""]]},"V934T":{"d":[["Vietnam","48490","mrgid","",""]]},"VB2ZF":{"d":[["Distribution. Uzbekistan (Semenov-Tian-Shanskij 1967).","","text","",""]]},"VB39F":{"d":[["DISTRIBUTION ET ÉCOLOGIE. — Rochers granitiques en bord de mer vers Andavaka, près de Fort-Dauphin. Cette plante pousse sur des inselbergs, dans une région très humide, versant Est de l’Andohahela.","","text","",""]]},"VCBW8":{"d":[["Peninsular Malaysia","48285","mrgid","",""]]},"VG3Z":{"d":[["Brazil","2143","mrgid","",""],["Brazil","2143","mrgid","",""],["Mato Grosso do Sul","48001","mrgid","native",""],["Mato Grosso do Sul","4